{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet7o951ZbymBcBRXwYym","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me summarize the analysis findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model (`Order.kt:11-16`) — currently has `orderId`, `customerId`, `amount`, `currency` but no status field\n- OrderController (`OrderController.kt`) — currently has `POST /orders` (create) and `GET /orders/{orderId}` endpoints\n- OrderRepository (`OrderRepository.kt`) — in-memory store using ConcurrentHashMap\n- Shipment model (`Shipment.kt:9-14`) — has `status: ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController (`ShipmentController.kt`) — currently has `POST /shipments` (create) and GET endpoints\n- ShipmentRepository (`ShipmentRepository.kt`) — in-memory store with no query by orderId\n- API error handling (`ApiExceptions.kt`, `ApiError.kt`, `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt`) — centralized exception handling with `ConflictException` (409) and `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n- ErrorCode enum (`ApiError.kt:31-37`) — currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them\n- `ConflictException` returns 409, `ResourceNotFoundException` returns 404\n- Tests use MockMvc with `mockMvc.perform()`, assert both status and error envelope code\n- Tests follow pattern: create state, call endpoint, assert response body, then GET and assert persisted state\n- Repositories have `clear()` method for test setup\n- Error responses use `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")` to assert the error code\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class (cannot avoid)\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (cannot avoid)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add method to find shipments by orderId (needed for cancel to find all shipments)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — add validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders (cannot avoid)\n5. `ApiError.kt` — may need to add new error codes for order cancellation scenarios (cannot avoid)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for cancel endpoint (cannot avoid)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests by changing Order model structure (all existing Order creations must include status)\n- Forgetting to cancel CREATED shipments when cancelling order\n- Not being idempotent (calling cancel twice should succeed, not fail on second call)\n- Not checking for CONFIRMED shipments before cancelling (must reject with 409)\n- Forgetting to check order cancellation status when creating shipments\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None identified — the ticket is clear on all cases mentioned.\n\nNow let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` enum field to Order data class. When creating a new order in OrderController, initialize it to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - If order already CANCELLED, succeeds without changes (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException (409) and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, sets order status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, persists and returns the order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to get all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the `create` endpoint, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED. If so, throw ConflictException (409). Also need to inject OrderRepository to check order status.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code for when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order (409 response).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add comprehensive tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200, persists CANCELLED status, cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Cancelling already CANCELLED order succeeds without changes\n   - Cancelling when CONFIRMED shipment exists returns 409, nothing changes\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n   - GET /orders shows CANCELLED status after cancellation\n   - Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n- Instead of adding status to Order model, could have used a separate OrderStatus table/map. This was rejected because: (a) it's overengineering for an in-memory store, (b) Order responses must include status for GET /orders/{orderId} to work, (c) the ticket expects the order returned by cancel endpoint to include the status.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path (cancel ACTIVE order):*\n- Request: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- Read: Order by orderId, all Shipments by orderId\n- Check: Order exists (404 if not), Order is ACTIVE or CANCELLED (idempotent), no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any)\n- Write: Set Order.status = CANCELLED, set Shipment.status = CANCELLED for all CREATED shipments\n- Response: 200 OK with updated Order object\n- Verification: GET /orders/{orderId} shows CANCELLED status, GET /shipments returns CANCELLED shipments\n\n*Idempotent cancel (already CANCELLED):*\n- Request: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- Read: Order by orderId\n- Check: Order is CANCELLED\n- Write: Nothing\n- Response: 200 OK with Order (unchanged)\n- Verification: State identical before and after\n\n*Conflict (CONFIRMED shipment exists):*\n- Request: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n- Read: Order by orderId, all Shipments by orderId\n- Check: Any CONFIRMED shipment\n- Write: Nothing (all-or-nothing)\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT with error code\n- Verification: GET /orders/{orderId} still ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged\n\n*Not found:*\n- Request: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (orderId doesn't exist)\n- Response: 404 NOT_FOUND with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\n*Shipment creation for cancelled order:*\n- Request: POST /shipments with orderId of CANCELLED order\n- Check: Order exists, Order is not CANCELLED\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT with ORDER_CANCELLED code if cancelled\n- Verification: No shipment created\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancels_an_active_order_with_created_shipments` — Create order + 2 shipments (CREATED and CONFIRMED), cancel order, verify order becomes CANCELLED in response, verify GET /orders shows CANCELLED, verify CREATED shipment became CANCELLED (CONFIRMED stays CONFIRMED), verify response body contains cancelled order\n2. `cancelling_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` — Create and cancel order, call cancel again, verify succeeds (200), verify response is identical, no state change\n3. `cancel_rejected_when_confirmed_shipment_exists` — Create order + CONFIRMED shipment, attempt cancel, verify 409, verify order still ACTIVE via GET, verify shipment still CONFIRMED\n4. `cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404` — Cancel non-existent orderId, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n5. `creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` — Create order, cancel it, attempt to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code, verify GET /shipments shows no shipment was created\n6. `newly_created_order_has_active_status` — Existing test or implicit in new tests — verify new orders start as ACTIVE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":20571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecbcd22d-202c-425a-a8a8-637fcc5ee6f8","uuid":"641132e1-7656-4f88-95e5-87544f95a2dc","timestamp":