orders must track their status and GET /orders must report it.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Added `cancel()` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 200 unchanged if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Returns 409 if any CONFIRMED shipment exists (all-or-nothing)\n   - Otherwise cancels order, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns 200 with cancelled order\n   - Injected ShipmentRepository to query shipments by orderId\n   This change was necessary for the core requirement.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId()` method to find all shipments for an order. Necessary for cancel endpoint to find shipments to cancel.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added validation in `create()` to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders with 409 ORDER_CANCELLED. Injected OrderRepository to check order status. Necessary to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes. Necessary for consistent error reporting.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new tests covering all scenarios (active order cancel, idempotent cancel, CONFIRMED shipment rejection, non-existent order, shipment cancel, new orders have ACTIVE status). Tests follow testing-and-verification pattern with separate GET requests after mutations and error assertions on error codes.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order. Tests follow the pattern with error code assertions.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with order status tracking, idempotent cancellation, CONFIRMED shipment blocking, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to track order lifecycle (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint implementing all cancellation logic\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 comprehensive tests for cancel endpoint covering all scenarios\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests:\n- `newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status()` — Verifies new orders start with ACTIVE status\n- `cancels_an_active_order_and_returns_200_with_cancelled_order()` — Tests happy path: order cancelled, persisted, and returned\n- `cancel_created_shipments_when_cancelling_order()` — Tests CREATED shipments are cancelled along with order\n- `cancelling_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_without_change()` — Tests idempotent behavior\n- `cancel_rejected_when_confirmed_shipment_exists_and_nothing_changes()` — Tests 409 rejection with no state change\n- `cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404()` — Tests 404 for unknown order\n- `rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_the_error_envelope()` — Tests 409 rejection when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` in sample-service/ — All 20 tests pass (10 OrderControllerTest + 6 ShipmentControllerTest + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests + 3 CustomerControllerTest), BUILD SUCCESS\n\nNot done: Nothing — all requirements implemented, tested, and verified.","ttft_ms":3690,"type":"result","duration_ms":179946,"uuid":"dec8b104-9e19-4528-9b8a-c006febd8e3b","ttft_stream_ms":744,"time_to_request_ms":31,"first_content_frame_ms":1058,"queued_turn_count":0}

